abstract: >
  ZEVAMPY is an open-source Python framework for vehicle stock turnover modelling using configurable vehicle-registration scenarios and survival assumptions. The framework supports survival-rate derivation from stock-by-age data, directly supplied empirical survival rates, and fitted cumulative survival probability parameters. Survival assumptions can be defined by country or by country and powertrain, and are combined with historical and projected registrations to estimate vehicle stock and stock shares over user-defined projection horizons.
